course: dictionary
lesson: 1705
title: One word, two drinks
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the place you are reading about can change which meaning is right. «Vinegar is water with acetic acid in it, made by bacteria from wine or cider.» Here cider is something that can be turned into vinegar, so it means a drink made from crushed apples.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. In the vinegar sentence, cider is an ingredient for making something sour, not a treat to share at a party. If you read about a hot drink on a frosty Halloween night, the clues point to a different meaning.
explain: Try the meaning in the sentence. Swap in "a drink made from crushed apples" and check that it still makes sense. When a word means different things in different countries, the dictionary tells you which meaning goes with which place.
fact: Cider is a drink made from the juice of crushed apples.
fact: In the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand, cider is an alcoholic drink, a bit like beer in strength.
fact: In the USA and Canada, cider is usually cloudy apple juice with no alcohol, often drunk hot in autumn.
fact: In North America, «hard cider» means cider that contains alcohol.
fact: Cider is usually uncountable, so you say «some cider», but you can say «two ciders» to mean two glasses or bottles.
exercise: «Vinegar is water with acetic acid in it, made by bacteria from wine or cider.» In this sentence, what is cider? | A jar used to store water | A kind of vinegar | *A drink made from crushed apples | A small fruit that grows on trees
exercise: A child in the USA asks for hot cider on a cold Halloween night. What is most likely in the cup? | Strong beer with a bitter taste | Milk with a cinnamon stick | Hot water with honey only | *Cloudy apple juice with no alcohol
exercise: What does «two ciders» mean? | Two apples cut in half | Two orchards in autumn | Two sweet cakes | *Two glasses or bottles of cider
test: In the UK, what is cider usually? | A hard sweet sold in shops | *An alcoholic drink, a bit like beer in strength | A small green apple | Cloudy apple juice with no alcohol, always served hot
test: In North America, what does «hard cider» mean? | A machine for pressing apples | Apple cider vinegar | *Cider that contains alcohol | Hot cider served at fairs
exam: «Vinegar is water with acetic acid in it, made by bacteria from wine or cider.» What can we learn about cider from this sentence? | Cider is never made from apples | Cider is a kind of bread | *Cider can be used to make vinegar | Cider is always served hot
